For a nonempty family of finite walks, $$\label{eq:el-traffic-identity}
 \mathop{\mathrm{EL}}_{\mathsf G}(\mathcal F)
 =\inf_{\mu}\mathcal T_{\mathsf G}(\mu),$$ where finite-support probability laws on $\mathcal F$ suffice for the infimum.

For each network, in each joint extraction there is a deterministic constant $k>0$, possibly depending on the extraction and on the choice of primal or dual, such that in every ordinary chart $$\label{eq:scalar-relaxation}
 \mathcal R(f,U)=k\int_U\lvert \nabla f\rvert^2\,\mathrm dx
 \qquad(f\in C(U)\cap H^1_{\rm loc}(U)).$$

At every such level with uniformly diverging view units, the common event above can be chosen so that, for every family of disjoint blocks and every vertex function, $$\label{eq:energy-overlap}
 \sum_I\mathcal E_m(f;W_I)
 \le C e^{N/40}\mathcal E_m(f;G_m^+).$$

Almost surely, the closure in $L^2(\mu_h)$ of the smooth form $\frac12\mathcal E^0$ has domain $$\label{eq:continuum-form-domain}
 \mathcal D_h=R_{\mu_h}(H^1(\mathbb S^2,\mathrm{vol}_0)),\qquad
 \mathcal E_h(R_{\mu_h}f,R_{\mu_h}g)=\frac12\mathcal E^0(f,g).$$

